<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Sèvres</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Sèvres was the peace treaty of 1920 between the Allied powers and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. It provided for the partition of much of the empire's remaining territory among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> and new states. Accounts of the Ottoman Empire treat it as a mark of the empire's final collapse; it was rejected by the Turkish nationalist movement and replaced by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-lausanne">Treaty of Lausanne</a> in 1923.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-sevres.jpg" alt="Treaty of Sèvres" width="297" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Collective · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Traitedepaix-sevres10081920-webaram.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1919 its troops landed at Smyrna, and the <b>Treaty of Sèvres</b> of 1920 seemed to fulfil the Great Idea, but the advance into Anatolia was halted at the Sakarya River in 1921, and in August 1922 the Turkish nationalist army routed the Greek forces.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-greece">Kingdom of Greece · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…stripped the empire of nearly all its remaining European territory, and its alignment with the Central Powers in the First World War, which led to the Allied occupation of Istanbul from 1918 and the punitive <b>Treaty of Sèvres</b> in 1920, created the conditions for Mustafa Kemal’s nationalist movement.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The Armistice of Mudros in 1918 and the <b>Treaty of Sèvres</b> of 1920 proposed the empire's partition, and the Allied occupation of Istanbul in 1918 and İzmir in 1919 set off the Turkish National Movement under Mustafa Kemal Pasha.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-turkey">Republic of Turkey · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>…was made during the Turkish War of Independence, when the Turkish National Movement led by Mustafa Kemal Atatürk was fighting both invading foreign powers and the Ottoman court, which it held to be complicit in the partition of the Turkish homeland after the <b>Treaty of Sèvres</b> of 1920.</blockquote><a href="/songs/istiklal-marsi">Independence March</a></li><li><blockquote>In November 1920 the Red Army invaded Armenia, only three months after the signing of the <b>Treaty of Sèvres</b>, which had recognised the country as a sovereign state.</blockquote><a href="/songs/mer-hayrenik">Mer Hayrenik (Our Fatherland)</a></li><li><blockquote>After the Ottoman defeat it expanded to Kars, and the <b>Treaty of Sevres</b> in 1920 promised it much of eastern Anatolia.</blockquote><a href="/state/first-republic-of-armenia">First Republic of Armenia</a></li></ul></section>
